      bullCase: "The bull case rests on a US CPI report that shows inflation moderating more significantly than anticipated, especially in Core CPI. Combined with dipping global oil prices, this could lead to a less aggressive Federal Reserve stance, potentially slowing the pace of rate hikes. Such a scenario would reduce recessionary fears, boost risk appetite globally, and attract FII inflows back into Indian equities, leading to a broad market rally.",
      bearCase: "The bear case involves a US CPI report that comes in hotter than expected, particularly Core CPI M/M at 0.3% or higher, triggering the Federal Reserve\'s commitment to a 50-basis point hike as indicated by Governor Waller. This aggressive tightening would likely lead to higher bond yields, a stronger US dollar, and a significant sell-off in global equities, including a sharp correction in Indian markets due to FII outflows and increased cost of capital.",
      neutralCase: "The neutral perspective suggests that the US CPI report will largely align with consensus expectations, leading to the anticipated 25-basis point rate hike by the Fed. Markets would likely absorb this outcome with moderate volatility, maintaining a \'wait-and-see\' approach for subsequent data. Oil prices could stabilize, and geopolitical tensions might remain contained, preventing any major shifts in sentiment but also limiting significant upside.",
