      bearCase: "A major security breach at a leading exchange like Binance will severely erode investor confidence, leading to a sustained sell-off in Bitcoin and altcoins. Increased regulatory pressure could stifle innovation and make it harder for exchanges to operate, creating a more restrictive environment that deters new investment and slows adoption.",
      neutralCase: "The market will experience immediate volatility and a dip in prices, but the long-term trajectory of Bitcoin is unlikely to be fundamentally altered. The industry will adapt with improved security, and while regulatory changes will occur, they may ultimately lead to a more stable and mature market, balancing the short-term negative impact with long-term structural improvements.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A short-to-medium term bearish outlook is highly probable (60%) due to market FUD and regulatory uncertainty. However, the long-term outlook leans neutral to cautiously bullish (40%) as the industry adapts and strengthens, demonstrating resilience akin to past recovery cycles from major security incidents.",
      potentialCatalysts: ["Binance\'s swift and transparent response with robust security upgrades.", "Industry-wide collaboration on new security standards and protocols.", "Clear and supportive regulatory frameworks that foster innovation while ensuring security.", "Renewed institutional investment demonstrating confidence in the long-term viability of crypto."],
